  "img": "icons/svg/book.svg",
  "system": {
    "identifier": "shadow-bite",
    "description": "<p>You create a single momentary needle of darkness that erupts upwards from a creature’s shadow that you can see within range.</p>\n<p>Make a ranged Genjutsu attack. On a hit you deal 4d6 psychic damage and the affected creature must make a Wisdom Saving throw.</p>\n<p>Success: Affected creature is able to resist most of this jutsu’s effects.</p>\n<p>Failure: Affected creature begin to see a shadow out of the corner of their eyes for the duration, always there, always just out of sight gaining 1 rank of Demoralized and reducing their speed by 10. An affected creature remakes the saving throw at the end of each of its turns to end their movement penalty effect.</p>\n<p>Critical Failure: Same as failure. But affected creature gains 2 ranks of Demoralized and reduces their speed by 15.</p>\n<p>At Higher Ranks: For each rank you cast this jutsu above D-Rank, increase the cost of this jutsu by 3, the number of creatures you can target by +1 and the damage by 1d6.</p>",
